{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"coding","tool":"read_file","arguments":{"name":"primary-publication-README.md"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"Reusable primary-publication lookup\\n\\nRun primary-publication.js with input {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"<PDB identifier>\\\"} using the coding run_code tool. The script performs credential-free public GET reads against RCSB GraphQL and Crossref works. It requires the requested entry to exist, RCSB's citation id to be primary, and a DOI to be present. It resolves that DOI through Crossref and requires a matching DOI, journal-article type, and matching normalized publication title. It returns entry_id, DOI, Crossref's exact title array, and publisher. These checks distinguish the primary publication from a structure dataset DOI. Any missing or inconsistent evidence throws an error; report UNABLE with the reason rather than inventing metadata. No entry-specific result is retained in this solution.\\n\""}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
